efinley%peruvian.utah.edu@cs.utah.edu (Elliott Finley) wrote:

>I haven't played nethack for about 1.5 years, and I can't remember
>what the ring of polymorph does...  

it randomly changes you into any one of the many monsters in the dungeon
(as long as the monster doesn't have a specific name).  this works best
with a ring of polymorph control ...

>             Other spoilers welcome

okay ... remember there is a random element (which may be affected by your
luck), you can end up changing into nymphs or other useless creatures,
but turning into a gray dragon, vampire lord or Olog-hai is fun, this is
why everyone searches for this combination of rings.

say you are a blue dragon, but getting walloped by Jubilex (a major demon),
once your hitpoints go to zero, you return to human form with the number
of hitpoints you had before you polymorphed.

also there is a danger of system shock when polymorphing without a ring of
polymorph control.  you just simply die (bummer).

a neat thing about polymorphing is sometimes you polymorph into another
person ("You feel like a new man!"), your class is the same, but you get
new stats, hitpoints and experience.  Again, I think luck influences this
so if your luck is good you gain levels pretty quick.
